#: includes/admin/documentation.php:226
msgid "Besides the Volunteer role, the plugin offers two roles for delegating day-to-day work without handing out full Administrator access:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:229
msgid "Role"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:230
msgid "Can do"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:234
#: includes/helpers.php:183
msgid "Volunteer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:235
msgid "Sign up for and cancel shifts, edit their own profile. No access to wp-admin beyond that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:238
#: includes/helpers.php:261
msgid "Volunteer Manager"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:239
msgid "Manage volunteers (edit their department links) and send announcements. Cannot create, edit, or delete shifts, and cannot access Import or Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:242
#: includes/helpers.php:257
msgid "Shift Manager"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:243
msgid "Everything Volunteer Manager can do, plus create, edit, and delete shifts and departments. Cannot access Import or Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:246
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:247
msgid "Full access to everything, including Import and Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:251
msgid "Assign a role under Users → All Users → edit the user → Role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:252
msgid "Important:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:252
msgid "a WordPress account can only have one role at a time through that Role dropdown — picking a new role there replaces the old one, it does not add to it. So switching an Administrator to Shift Manager or Volunteer Manager removes their Administrator access; only do this for accounts that should not have full admin access. The one exception is the Volunteer role: use the \"Grant volunteer role\" / \"Remove role\" buttons on the Volunteers page instead of the Role dropdown to add or remove it without disturbing whatever other role the account already has — for example, to let a Shift Manager or Volunteer Manager also show up on the Volunteers page itself, so they can be assigned to a shift or receive department-targeted announcements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:255
msgid "Departments (Manager → Departments) group shifts, can be nested under a parent, and each carries a color used for its badge on shift cards and in the overview. \"Hide from volunteers\" removes a department from the frontend filter and labels; a shift disappears for volunteers only when every department it belongs to is hidden (shifts someone already signed up for are never hidden). Color, parent, visibility, and description can also be changed via Quick Edit in the department list, and the shift list itself can be filtered and sorted by department."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:259
msgid "Adding a department: nest it under a parent to build a hierarchy, give it a color for its badges, and optionally hide it from volunteers without deleting it — shifts already assigned there stay visible to the people on them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:261
msgid "Open Departments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:269
msgid "Once shifts exist, this is where you'll spend most of your time: watching sign-ups, managing volunteers, and keeping everyone informed. Most of the rules mentioned below — registration behavior, shift limits, overlap prevention, spam protection — live on one screen, Shifts → Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:273
msgid "Settings → General: whether WordPress sends its own \"set your password\" email, and the shift-limit rules (per day/week/month/year, overlap prevention, cancellation deadline). Scroll further on this tab for the admin-menu and CAPTCHA options mentioned in the FAQ below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:275
#: includes/admin/getting-started-checklist.php:201
#: includes/admin/getting-started-checklist.php:261
msgid "Open Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:281
msgid "The [eventadmin] page offers two ways in, so people can pick whichever is faster for them — neither is required for the other to work:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:283
msgid "Social login"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:283
msgid "install the free Nextend Social Login plugin and configure at least one provider (Google, Facebook, and X are included free) and its buttons appear above the registration form automatically — no code or shortcode changes needed. One click, no form to fill in: the easiest option for anyone who already has one of those accounts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:284
msgid "Magic login link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:284
msgid "everyone else fills in name, phone, and email and gets a one-time login link by email instead of a password (see the FAQ below). No account to remember, and no \"forgot password\" flow to support — this is what makes the plugin usable for occasional, one-off volunteers who won't want to set up a login just for one shift."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:286
msgid "Both create the same volunteer account underneath. Someone who registers via Google still receives the same assignment and reminder emails, shows up once on the Volunteers page, and is badged \"Social\" there (see Volunteer List & Badges below) so you can see at a glance how each volunteer signed up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:290
msgid "The [eventadmin] page as a logged-in volunteer sees it: shifts they've already joined at the top (\"My shifts\"), then everything still open to sign up for below — department, time, spots left, and who else is already on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:292
msgid "Open your volunteer page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:298
msgid "The shift overview (Shifts → Overview) is split into four tabs, each showing only the filters relevant to it:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:300
msgid "registered volunteers, upcoming shifts, and open spots split into required (below a shift's minimum) and optional (up to the maximum)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:301
msgid "Cards"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:301
msgid "the shift cards, with filters for upcoming/past/all, department, volunteer, and date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:302
msgid "a flat, export-style table; the \"Add volunteer\" button assigns someone without leaving the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:303
msgid "Timeline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:303
msgid "a per-volunteer Gantt chart. Drag a shift's bar to move or resize it (with an Undo after saving), or use the Edit Shift modal for exact times. Unfilled slots show as red (below minimum) or grey (optional) bars, which can be toggled off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/documentation.php:308
msgid "The Timeline tab for one day: one row per volunteer, coloured bars for their shifts, and grey/red bars for the slots still open. Drag a bar sideways to reschedule it."
msgstr ""

